# Repository Guidelines

<!-- BEGIN JIG MANAGED BLOCK -->
This repository uses the shared `jig.sh` workflow. Keep repo-local business rules and ownership guidance in [% if rust_workspace_guidance_enabled %]crate-level[% else %]backend-level[% endif %] guides; keep generic agent workflow and repo policy here.

## Start Here

- Open [agent-map.md](./agent-map.md) before [% if rust_workspace_guidance_enabled %]Rust[% else %]backend[% endif %] work.
- Read the nearest [% if rust_workspace_guidance_enabled %]crate-level[% else %]backend-level[% endif %] `AGENTS.md` before changing a [% if rust_workspace_guidance_enabled %]crate[% else %]package or crate[% endif %] when one exists.
- Use `.agent/PLANS.md` when writing an ExecPlan for a complex feature or refactor.
- Use `scripts/jig` for the typed repo contract and `scripts/jig mcp` for MCP clients. Discover targets with `scripts/jig info targets`; preview verification with `scripts/jig check --explain`.
- On a fresh machine, run `scripts/jig doctor`; follow its next step, including `scripts/jig agent bootstrap` when Jig Codex skills are missing.
[% if not rust_workspace_guidance_enabled -%]
- Run local services with `scripts/jig dev` to use the repository's proxy and port configuration.
[% endif -%]
- For substantial work, use `scripts/jig work start`, then `scripts/jig work check --plan-id <id>` and `scripts/jig work finish --plan-id <id> --resolution "..."`. Use `scripts/jig work gates`, `evidence`, `receipts`, or `status` for diagnostics when needed.
[% if _jig.contract_version >= 6 -%]
- Plans capture an exact Git baseline. `work check` reuses current passing target evidence when its freshness policy allows and reruns checks that need new evidence. Required gate policies still govern `work finish`.
[% else -%]
- Plans capture an exact Git baseline. Default `work check` runs required gates whose configured path policy applies and records explicit not-applicable evidence for the rest; `work finish` enforces required gates.
[% endif -%]
- `jig-contract` validates Jig harness wiring, not the application's API contract.
- Treat `.agent/state/*.jsonl` as append-only repo memory.

## Compatibility And Cutovers

- Prefer direct cutovers only for internal code-only changes that can ship in one coordinated deploy.
- Preserve compatibility or stage rollouts for persisted database state, queued job types, public API contracts, bookmarked routes, webhook boundaries, or source-of-truth moves that can straddle deploys.
[% if sqlx_enabled %]
[% if rust_migration_layout == "flat_migrations" %]
- Never overwrite an existing database migration; add a new forward-only migration instead.
[% else %]
- The migration tree contains complete versioned schema artifacts. Never overwrite a shipped version; add the next forward-only version and its repository-owned cutover artifact.
[% endif %]
[% else %]
[% if go_postgres_enabled %]
- Never overwrite an existing database migration; add a new forward-only migration instead.
[% endif %]
[% endif %]

## [% if rust_workspace_guidance_enabled %]Rust[% else %]Backend[% endif %] Defaults

[% if go_backend_enabled %]
- Treat `cmd/` as process entrypoints and `internal/` as private application packages.
- Add package-level `AGENTS.md` files when a package has meaningful ownership, entrypoint, or invariant guidance that should travel with that package.
- Keep transport logic thin and business logic in the owning package.
- Keep the Huma API constructor free of database connections, listeners, and other process lifecycle work so `cmd/openapi` remains offline.
[% if go_postgres_enabled %]
- Embedded Goose migrations live under `internal/database/migrations/`; sqlc queries and committed generated code live under `internal/database/queries/` and `internal/database/sqlc/`.
- Add migrations with `scripts/jig migration add NAME`; verify generated SQL code with `scripts/jig check sqlc`.
- Use pgxpool for application traffic and keep Goose's `database/sql` adapter short-lived.
[% endif %]
[% endif %]
[% if rust_backend_enabled %]
- Treat [% for root in rust_crate_roots %]`<<[ root ]>>`[% if not loop.last %], [% endif %][% endfor %] as Rust crate roots.
- Add crate-level `AGENTS.md` files when a crate has meaningful ownership, entrypoint, or invariant guidance that should travel with that crate.
[% if not rust_workspace_guidance_enabled %]
- Keep transport logic thin and business logic in the owning crate.
[% endif %]
[% endif %]
[% if sqlx_enabled %]
[% if rust_migration_layout == "flat_migrations" %]
- SQL migrations live under `<<[ migration_dir ]>>`; add them with `scripts/jig migration add NAME`.
[% else %]
- Versioned SQL schema artifacts live under `<<[ migration_dir ]>>`; do not use `scripts/jig migration add` in this layout.
[% endif %]
- SQLx metadata is committed in `<<[ rust_sqlx_metadata_dir ]>>`.
[% if schema_dump_enabled %]
- Refresh schema documentation with `scripts/jig sqlx schema dump`.
[% endif %]
[% endif %]
[% if sqlx_enabled %]
- Keep transaction boundaries explicit and deterministic.
[% endif %]

## Frontend Defaults

[% if frontend_apps | length > 0 -%]
Configured web apps:

[% for app in frontend_apps -%]
- `<<[ app.name ]>>` in `<<[ app.dir ]>>`
[% endfor %]

Each configured app is expected to support `lint`, `typecheck`, `build:bundle`, and `test:coverage`.
[% if _jig.contract_version >= 6 -%]
Structured work verifies the configured repository profile, including its frontend targets.
[% else -%]
Structured work uses configured check gates; repository-wide TypeScript checks remain available for an intentional full-matrix run.
[% endif -%]
[% if application_contracts_enabled -%]
For application contract freshness and public deployment boundaries, use `scripts/check-webapps.sh application-contracts` and `scripts/check-webapps.sh public-artifacts`.
[% endif -%]
`test:coverage` must write `coverage/coverage-summary.json` in the app directory for threshold enforcement.
Jig validates those scripts during adoption; generated web CI validates them again before running.
Run package scripts through `scripts/check-webapps.sh run-script <app-dir> <script>`.
Install scope follows package-manager workspace membership; keep registry, authentication, and install-script policy project-owned.
`[[frontend_apps]]` owns CI and coverage metadata; matching `[[dev.apps]]` entries own local development. Extra dev apps have no generated web CI. Replace legacy `dev_command` with `[dev]` and `[[dev.apps]]`.
`kind` selects `vite` or `env-port`; `role` selects `spa`, `admin`, or `astro`.
[% else -%]
No web apps are configured in `.jig.toml`.
[% endif %]

## Done Means

- Run the relevant local verification for the area you changed.
- For [% if rust_workspace_guidance_enabled %]Rust[% else %]backend[% endif %] changes, finish with `scripts/jig check test`.
[% if frontend_apps | length > 0 %]
- For frontend changes, run the relevant `scripts/jig check typescript-*` gates.
[% endif %]
[% if sqlx_enabled %]
- For SQLx or migration changes, run `scripts/jig check sqlx`.
[% if schema_dump_enabled %]
- For schema-doc-enabled repos, run `scripts/jig check schema`.
[% endif %]
[% endif %]
- Review the generated diff for stale docs, policy drift, or missing dependent updates.

